# tasksel machinery + tasks — debian-cd's update_tasks needs task-desktop and
# tasksel-data present in the CD mirror to build the task structure and derive
# the default desktop; task-kde-desktop pulls the full KDE closure the preseed's
# `tasksel/first ... kde-desktop` selects at install time (all of it offline).
tasksel
tasksel-data
task-desktop
task-kde-desktop
kde-plasma-desktop
sddm
konsole
dolphin
firefox-esr
network-manager
sudo
lvm2
grub-efi-amd64
efibootmgr
linux-image-6.12.0
linux-headers-6.12.0
sovereign-os-cockpit
python3
python3-yaml
python3-jsonschema
prometheus-node-exporter
curl
git
nano
# debian-cd's installtools step wants the installation guide present in the pool
installation-guide-amd64
# trixie's base-installer installs `zstd` as part of the base set (dpkg's default
# compressor), but nothing in the closure above depends on the zstd BINARY package
# (they pull libzstd1), so it was absent from the offline mirror and base-install
# failed with "Unable to install zstd". Pull it in explicitly.
zstd

# FIRMWARE. The custom kernel is CONFIG_DRM_AMDGPU=m / CONFIG_EXTRA_FIRMWARE="",
# so amdgpu loads at runtime and needs its blobs on disk. The Ryzen 9 9900X has
# a Granite Ridge iGPU [1002:13c0]; without these the installed system halts at
# "amdgpu: Fatal error during GPU init" right after a successful install
# (2026-07-26). mirror_files_include already carries non-free-firmware.
amd64-microcode
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-nvidia-graphics
firmware-linux-free
firmware-misc-nonfree

# ── THE SHARED INSTALLED-SYSTEM SET ─────────────────────────────────────────
# scripts/install/lib/installed-system.sh is the ONE definition of what an
# installed sovereign-os IS. This list had drifted 33 packages away from it:
# no xserver-xorg-video-fbdev/vesa (the ONLY X config proven on this hardware —
# no kernel driver binds to any of the three GPUs, the desktop runs on the EFI
# framebuffer), no systemd-resolved, and none of the console or hardware tools.
# That drift is what "it did load some GUI but it was buggy and there was not
# even a console tool installed" was (2026-07-26).
# tests/lint/test_installer_matches_the_installed_system.py keeps them in sync.
bash-completion
bind9-dnsutils
ca-certificates
console-setup
dmidecode
file
htop
initramfs-tools
iproute2
iputils-ping
isc-dhcp-client
keyboard-configuration
less
lm-sensors
locales
lshw
lsof
man-db
ncdu
netbase
nvme-cli
pciutils
rsync
smartmontools
systemd-resolved
tmux
tree
usbutils
vim
wget
xserver-xorg-video-fbdev
xserver-xorg-video-vesa
xterm

# Step 08-image-sign instructs the operator to enroll the MOK cert with
# mokutil after install; it must therefore be ON the disc (2026-07-27).
mokutil

# xdg-utils — REQUIRED BY THE DASHBOARDS DEPLOY, and it was in neither list.
# install-gui-dashboards.sh pkg_ensure's xdg-utils for EVERY frontend
# (kde-plasma, gnome, xfce, kiosk). It was absent from this mirror list and from
# pkgsel/include, so on the offline install apt had no candidate for it:
#     E: Package 'xdg-utils' has no installation candidate
#     FAILED (rc=100)
# and the whole cockpit/dashboards deploy died with it -- silently, because
# late_command swallows the failure. Recovered from the failed disk's own
# /var/log/sovereign-os/dashboards-install.log (2026-07-28).
xdg-utils

# ── Priority: standard ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The "standard system utilities" task. tasksel selects it by priority, but
# an OFFLINE install can only install what the CD carries -- so the pool must
# hold them explicitly. Regenerate against a release with:
#   grep-aptavail -FPriority standard -sPackage | awk '{print $2}' | sort -u
apt-listchanges
bind9-host
bzip2
dbus
debian-faq
doc-debian
gettext-base
groff-base
inetutils-telnet
intel-microcode
krb5-locales
libc-l10n
liblockfile-bin
libnss-systemd
libpam-systemd
libpam-wtmpdb
manpages
media-types
ncurses-term
netcat-traditional
openssh-client
perl
reportbug
systemd-timesyncd
traceroute
ucf
util-linux-extra
wamerican
wtmpdb
xz-utils

# ── AI / driver enablement ──────────────────────────────────────────
# dkms + a compiler are what let nvidia-driver-install.sh build the module
# against the custom znver5 kernel on an OFFLINE first boot.
dkms
build-essential
pkg-config
python3-pip
python3-venv
python3-dev
